title: Spring Ring Campaign - Teams Social Engineering Reconnaissance Commands
id: c9a5d3e6-14b8-5f0c-d7a3-5e9b1c4f0a6d
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects reconnaissance commands executed after Spring Ring campaign
    actors gain remote access via Microsoft Teams social engineering
    (gbhackers, 2026). Attackers impersonate IT support, use Quick Assist
    or third-party RMM tools, then run whoami /groups, net group /dom,
    and PowerShell to download a RAT from san-sid.com. A second variant
    uses NTLM relay techniques after obtaining NTLMv2 hashes.
references:
    - https://gbhackers.com
    - https://cyberpress.org
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/09/02
tags:
    - attack.t1059
    - attack.t1219
    - attack.t1087
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_recon_whoami:
        Image|endswith: '\whoami.exe'
        CommandLine|contains: '/groups'
    selection_recon_net:
        Image|endswith: '\net.exe'
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'group /dom'
            - 'group /domain'
    selection_rmm_download:
        Image|endswith:
            - '\powershell.exe'
            - '\pwsh.exe'
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'san-sid.com'
            - 'Invoke-WebRequest'
            - 'DownloadString'
    condition: selection_recon_whoami or selection_recon_net or selection_rmm_download
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate IT administration performing group enumeration
    - RMM tools performing similar reconnaissance during authorized remote sessions
level: high
